{"word": "crazy", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "crazy", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "adjective", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈkɹeɪ.zi/", "tags": ["General American", "Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈkɹæɪ.zi/", "tags": ["General Australian"]}], "forms": [{"word": "crazier", "tags": ["comparative"]}, {"word": "craziest", "tags": ["superlative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "Of unsound mind; insane; demented.", "tags": [], "examples": ["His ideas were both frightening and crazy."], "quotes": [{"text": "Those words appearing to be merely the ravings of superannuation, they were not regarded; but when no other traces of Mary could be found, old Andrew went up to consult this crazy dame once more, but he was not able to bring any such thing to her recollection.", "reference": "1828, James Hogg, Mary Burnet:"}, {"text": "Of all the queer collections of humans outside of a crazy asylum, it seemed to me this sanitarium was the cup winner. […] When you're well enough off so's you don't have to fret about anything but your heft or your diseases you begin to get queer, I suppose.", "reference": "1913, Joseph C[rosby] Lincoln, chapter V, in Mr. Pratt’s Patients, New York, N.Y.; London: D[aniel] Appleton and Company, →OCLC:"}, {"text": "Now think of all the years you tried to\nFind someone to satisfy you\nI might be as crazy as you say\nIf I'm crazy then it's true\nThat it's all because of you\nAnd you wouldn't want me any other way", "reference": "1980 March 7, Billy Joel, “You May Be Right”, in Glass Houses:"}, {"text": "Grab-a-cop-gun kinda crazy / She's poison but tasty / Yeah, people say \"Run, don't walk, away\"", "reference": "2018, Ava Max, Madison Love, Tix, Cook Classics, Cirkut, “Sweet but Psycho”, in Heaven & Hell, performed by Ava Max:"}], "synonyms": ["5150", "bananas", "barking", "barking mad", "buggish", "buggy", "bughouse", "barmy", "batchy", "batpoop", "bats